      "rev_n_1_9011aa_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_9011aa_0",
        "node_id": "n_1_9011aa",
        "thought_text": "Since there are only 3 tasks, there are exactly 3! = 6 possible completion orders. I can iterate through all permutations, calculate the cost for each (0 + |A_j - A_i| + |A_k - A_j|), and find the minimum.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506489.0481718
      },
      "rev_n_2_6d634b_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_6d634b_0",
        "node_id": "n_2_6d634b",
        "thought_text": "Sort the array A. The optimal strategy likely involves completing tasks in sorted order (either ascending or descending) to minimize the sum of absolute differences between adjacent elements in the sequence.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506489.048187
      },
      "rev_n_3_42f004_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_42f004_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_42f004",
        "thought_text": "Analyze the mathematical property: the total cost is the sum of distances between consecutive tasks in the chosen path. For small N, brute force is safer than deriving a general formula to avoid edge cases.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506489.0481954
      },
      "rev_n_4_8b1a87_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_8b1a87_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_8b1a87",
        "thought_text": "Iterate through all 6 permutations of the 3 tasks, calculate the cumulative cost for each sequence (0 + |A_j - A_i| + |A_k - A_j|), and select the minimum.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8289531635937900559",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506512.5379052
