      "rev_n_5_7224d4_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_7224d4_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_7224d4",
        "thought_text": "Sort the array A. The optimal strategy for minimizing the sum of absolute differences between adjacent elements in a sequence is to visit them in sorted order (either ascending or descending).",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8289531635937900559",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506512.5379293
      },
      "rev_n_6_6c0e4f_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_6c0e4f_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_6c0e4f",
        "thought_text": "Since the constraints are extremely small (N=3), a brute-force approach checking every possible starting task and every subsequent path is computationally trivial and guarantees finding the global minimum without needing to prove sorting optimality.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-8289531635937900559",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506512.5379431
      },
      "rev_n_7_3425b8_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_7_3425b8_0",
        "node_id": "n_7_3425b8",
        "thought_text": "Since N=3 is very small, iterate through all 3! = 6 possible permutations of task completion orders and calculate the total cost for each, then take the minimum.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-4714163176196579991",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506521.1583219
      },
      "rev_n_8_9153ec_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_8_9153ec_0",
        "node_id": "n_8_9153ec",
        "thought_text": "Sort the array A first. The optimal path for minimizing sum of absolute differences on a line usually involves visiting the median element first or last, so check paths starting from the sorted median and moving outwards.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-4714163176196579991",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506521.158339
      },
      "rev_n_9_cb6fc4_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_9_cb6fc4_0",
        "node_id": "n_9_cb6fc4",
        "thought_text": "Use dynamic programming where dp[i][mask] represents the minimum cost to complete the set of tasks in 'mask' ending with task 'i', but given N=3, this is overkill compared to brute force.",
