      "rev_n_13_220fac_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_13_220fac_0",
        "node_id": "n_13_220fac",
        "thought_text": "Since N=3 is very small, I can generate all 6 permutations of task indices, calculate the cost for each sequence (0 + |A[j]-A[i]| + |A[k]-A[j]|), and take the minimum.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-279361933160324695",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506563.165464
      },
      "rev_n_14_56b61f_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_14_56b61f_0",
        "node_id": "n_14_56b61f",
        "thought_text": "Sort the array A first. The optimal strategy for minimizing the sum of absolute differences between adjacent elements in a sequence is to visit them in sorted order (either ascending or descending). I can just check the cost of the sorted sequence and the reverse sorted sequence.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-279361933160324695",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506563.1654806
      },
      "rev_n_15_e56c31_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_15_e56c31_0",
        "node_id": "n_15_e56c31",
        "thought_text": "Mathematically, the total cost for any permutation is the sum of distances between consecutive points. For points on a line, the minimum path visiting all points starts at one extreme and ends at the other, covering the range exactly once. The cost is simply max(A) - min(A).",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-279361933160324695",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794506563.1654897
      },
      "rev_n_16_b4c1a6_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_16_b4c1a6_0",
        "node_id": "n_16_b4c1a6",
        "thought_text": "Since N=3, there are only 6 possible permutations of task completion orders. I can iterate through all permutations, calculate the cost for each (0 + |A_j - A_i| + |A_k - A_j|), and find the minimum.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5169056160139059635",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
